# Loaded by `next dev` only. Committed on purpose: without it every "Sign in" link on the
# local site points at `app.careos.example`, which RFC 2606 guarantees will never resolve, and
# the first thing anyone does with a marketing site is click its primary call to action.
#
# `next build` does not read this file, so the placeholder remains the default for a production
# export — see the reasoning in src/content/site.ts. To point a build somewhere real, set
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ORIGIN in the build environment or in .env.production; to point your own dev
# server somewhere else, put it in .env.local, which is gitignored and wins over this file.
#
# Origin only. A path, a query, or a trailing slash is rejected or trimmed at build time rather
# than concatenated into a broken URL.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
